CORE
main.c
--unwind 5
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^field sensitivity was not applied to 1 array of structs, unions or pointers with more than 64 elements:$
^  adapter\.rings \(65 elements\)$
^.*Use --max-field-sensitivity-array-size 65 to apply field sensitivity to all of them; this limit applies to arrays of any element type
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^  scalar_buffer \(
--
An array of 65 structs holding a pointer exceeds the default field-sensitivity
limit of 64 and is reported, naming the array and the limit that would cover
it.  The 4096-element char array is also over the limit but holds no fields or
pointers, so it is not reported.
